# Language coverage on every function (always)

Resume: `@lang-coverage$` / `$language-coverage$`. Same standing as `floqr-translation.mdc`: **do not wait for the owner to ask.** Chrome/help key counts stay in that rule; **this rule is behavior** (matching, filters, Place SMARTview).

Owner (26 Nov 2026): city detection was Latin-only while **BOT DEE** UI is 11 languages. That is **poor design**. Always consider the other languages so the function does not fail.

## Supported languages (all required)

`en`, `de`, `fr`, `es`, `it`, `pt`, `ru`, `el`, `pl`, `nl`, `ar`

Incomplete language coverage is a **product bug**, not a follow-up. Shipping English/Latin tokens only (Miami vs ميامي / Μαϊάμι / Майами) while BOT DEE chrome is localized **fails this rule**.

## When this applies

Any **new or changed** function, matcher, token list, leftover-word filter, or “if the user said X” gate — especially:

- BOT DEE city / destination detection (`matchPlaces` / `CITY_HITS` in `functions/bot-dee-tools.js`)
- Place SMARTview attach, Search SMARTnotification place tags
- Venue / club haystack search, discovery city aliases (`CITY_ALIAS_GROUPS`)
- Intent search aliases, cuisine/stop-word lists, greeting skip lists used as gates

**s3.3.085 (owner asked):** Master Admin → Features Mgmt → BOT DEE → City / place tokens. Language required. Add translates via packaged aliases (never Gemini). Firestore `botDeeCityTokens`. `executeBotSession` reads the list.

## Required before calling the work done

1. **Ask how it behaves in every supported language**, including native scripts (Arabic, Greek, Cyrillic), not only Latin spellings (Milano, Lisboa, Cancún).
2. **Keep native-script aliases on the same token** as the Latin id (`miami`, `bali`, …). `\b` is ASCII-word only — do not rely on it around Arabic/Greek/Cyrillic.
3. **Do not Latin-strip the needle before matching** unless you also match the original string. `normalizeNeedle` today drops non `[a-z0-9]` (`functions/bot-dee-tools.js`) — that is why ميامي / Μαϊάμι / Майами never hit `CITY_HITS`. Changing a city list without fixing fold/strip is still Latin-only.
4. **Tests** must include at least one native-script prompt per new city/place token (ar + el + ru for Miami/Bali-class destinations). Chrome i18n key-count green is **not** enough.
5. Protected brands stay untranslated (**BOT DEE**, ShoutOut, FloqR, SMARTview, …). Place names may have native aliases; brands never do.

## Shipped matcher (s3.3.085)

`functions/botdee-city-tokens.js` packaged aliases (11 langs) + Firestore overlay. `normalizePlaceNeedle` keeps `\p{L}`. Unicode boundaries, not ASCII `\b`. Tests cover ميامي / Μαϊάμι / Майами.

## Checklist (mental, every function iteration)

- [ ] Matcher/token/stop lists considered for all 11 langs (not only `CHROME.*` keys)
- [ ] Native-script aliases where patrons will type them; ASCII `\b` not the only boundary
- [ ] Needle fold does not delete the scripts you claim to match
- [ ] Tests for ar / el / ru (and Latin aliases already in the list)
- [ ] City-token admin (when present) requires language pick + SOS2FA + reason; no Gemini auto-learn

